---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import BandOverview from '../../components/BandOverview.astro';
import { u, bands, BAND_INFO } from '../../lib/data';
const B = bands();
---
<Base title="Curriculum and timeline" description="Two age groups, three levels each: what students learn, the timeline, example projects and how progress is measured.">
  <div class="measure stack">
    <p class="eyebrow">Curriculum</p>
    <h1>Two age groups, one clear path</h1>
    <p class="lead">The course has a track for Grades 2–3 and a track for Grades 4–6, with three levels each and one session a week. Every level has the same rhythm and ends with a project your child designs, builds and shows.</p>
    <nav aria-label="Jump to an age group"><ul class="chips">{B.map((b) => <li><a class="pill" href={`#${b.id}`}>{b.band_title}: {BAND_INFO[b.id].short}</a></li>)}</ul></nav>
  </div>

  {B.map((b) => (
    <section class="band-section" aria-labelledby={b.id} style="margin-top:3rem">
      <div class="measure stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">{b.band_title} · ages {b.ages}</p>
        <h2 id={b.id}>{BAND_INFO[b.id].short}</h2>
        <p>{BAND_INFO[b.id].blurb} Three levels, {BAND_INFO[b.id].session}.</p>
        <p><a href={u(`${b.id}/`)}>All about {b.band_title} <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p>
      </div>
      <BandOverview band={b} h={3} />
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="measure stack" style="margin-top:3rem" aria-labelledby="progress">
    <h2 id="progress">How progress is measured</h2>
    <p>Through projects, rubrics and friendly checkpoints, never grades. In Grades 4–6, rubrics have four levels: <em>Just starting</em>, <em>Getting there</em>, <em>Got it</em> and <em>Expert</em>. In Grades 2–3, a grown-up watches and ticks a short show-me checklist: <em>Not yet</em>, <em>Getting there</em> or <em>Got it</em>. Creativity, working code and the ability to explain it count equally.</p>
    <p>Parents: see <a href={u('parents/#assessment')}>how progress is checked</a> and <a href={u('parents/research/')}>what the research says</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
